# Registration forms — guest and member

FRM (`components/forms/frm/`) is the **reference implementation**. Every other
programme form — SCR, RAI/RAIJ, FRR, FFR, affiliate — follows the shape
described here. Read this before starting any of them.

This rule assumes `legacy-rewrite.md` (which repo is which), `commands.md`
(where to run builds), `project-structure.md` (the four component tiers) and
`theming.md` (tokens only). It does not repeat them.

---

## 0. The order that works

FRM took as long as it did because most of the list below was discovered rather
than planned. Follow the sequence; each step points at the section that explains
it.

1. **Read GarpAppv1 for this programme** (§1) — endpoints and their order, exact
   field list, validation character-for-character, and every `isAuthenticated`
   branch. Retrieve the deployed copy, not the local checkout.
2. **Read the Apex for what no client can tell you** (§1, §8) — what is
   actually required, what is validated server-side, what is not idempotent.
3. **Diff the programme against FRM before writing anything.** Almost all the
   machinery is shared (§3). What is usually genuinely new: the programme's
   title and `publicByLine`, its policy URL, which sections apply at all, and
   whether it has study materials or shipping.
4. **Wire the route pair and guards** (§2) — member under `_appLayout`, public
   under `_publicFormLayout`. Do not add a layout group.
5. **Build from the shared pieces** (§3) — reuse the hooks, payload builders and
   pure rules; add only the sections this programme needs.
6. **Account for every field the payload sends** (§5) — anything
   `buildRegisterRequest` puts on the wire with no control behind it is being
   posted as its default, silently.
7. **Wire the cross-field effects** (§6) — the billing country is the one that
   bites, and it has two entry points.
8. **Work the checklist** (§8), both audiences, in a browser.

